DWHENCE(1)                     ZOAU Command Syntax                    DWHENCE(1)

NAME

	dwhence - Search for a member within a dataset concatenation.

SYNOPSIS

	dwhence [-dhv] <MEMBER> <CONCATENATION>

	-d
		Print out debug messages.

	-h
		Display syntax help.

	-j
		Print output in JSON format.

	-J
		Print JSON output in a readable format.

	-v
		Print out verbose command information.

DESCRIPTION

	Search for a dataset MEMBER within a dataset CONCATENATION.
	dwhence supports the generation dataset relative name notation.

EXAMPLES

	Look for dataset member TEST within a dataset concatenation:

		dwhence TEST DATASET.ONE:DATASET.TWO:DATASET.THREE

	Search for member DATA in a dataset concatenation and get JSON output:

		dwhence -J DATA DATASET.ONE:DATASET.TWO:DATASET.THREE

		{
			"data": {
					"found": true,
					"result": "JURIBE.TEST.PDS",
					"member": "DATA",
					"search_list": [
							"DATASET.ONE",
							"DATASET.TWO",
							"DATASET.THREE"
					]
			},
			"program": "dwhence",
			"options": "-J ",
			"rc": "0"
		}

EXIT VALUES

	0
		Success.

	8
		No matches were found.

	Other
		Error, see message for details.
